# ---- derived / regenerable working data (see RESTORATION.md §6) -------------
# Decoded sources (245 MB), per-song stems (968 MB), separation inputs,
# ONNX model download, transient plots and logs are all reproducible with
# work/run_separation.py + work/run_all_restore.sh, and would blow up the repo,
# so they are not tracked.
work/src/
work/prep/
work/stems/
# the ONNX separator weights (174 MB) are downloadable, but the trained
# top-octave networks are 80 KB each and are part of the deliverable
work/models/htdemucs.onnx
work/logs/
work/plots/
work/__pycache__/
work/*.log
work/report.json

# ---- audio deliverables ----------------------------------------------------
# Everything a listener is told to download must actually be in the repo.
# This used to ignore restored/*.wav, which silently excluded the 24-bit WAV
# masters AND the A/B excerpts - the one file a listener is most likely to open -
# while RESTORATION.md documented them as deliverables. The FLAC masters cover
# lossless audio, but the A/B excerpts have no lossless equivalent elsewhere, so
# they are tracked; the redundant 24-bit WAV duplicate of the FLAC is not kept
# (it is ~48 MB per song at the same resolution as the FLAC).
restored/*.wav
!restored/*(A-B 30s).wav
masters/*.wav

# ---- misc ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
